From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:01:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Report Apple GPUs with their Metal GPU family as device ID.

Wine's Mac driver registers the display adapter with the highest
MTLGPUFamilyApple value as its PCI device ID, while MoltenVK combined
OS version and GPU families into a 32-bit value. Windows games that
match the adapter DXGI reports against the display devices, such as
Ratchet & Clank: Rift Apart, then found no graphics card.
---
 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
index f8e48c4..5a5a49f 100644
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
@@ -3146,7 +3146,11 @@ void MVKPhysicalDevice::initGPUInfoProperties() {
 	// of from the build, in case we are running Rosetta2.
 	if (_gpuCapabilities.isAppleGPU) {
 		_properties.vendorID = kAppleVendorId;
-		_properties.deviceID = getHighestGPUCapability();
+		// Report the highest Apple GPU family as its MTLGPUFamilyApple value, which is what Wine's Mac
+		// driver registers as the display adapter's device ID. Windows games match the adapter that
+		// DXGI reports against the display devices and find no GPU when the IDs differ.
+		uint8_t gpuA = _gpuCapabilities.getHighestAppleGPU();
+		_properties.deviceID = gpuA ? MTLGPUFamilyApple1 - 1 + gpuA : getHighestGPUCapability();
 		return;
 	}
 
